Life Cycle of File in Git:
--------------------------
-Every file in Git is in one of the following states:
1)Untracked state:
-----------------
-The files which are newly created in working directory and git does not aware of these files are said to be in untracked state.

2)Staged state:
---------------
-The files which are added to staging area said to be staged state.
-These files are ready for commit.
3)InRepository/Commited:
------------------------
-Any file which is commited is said to be InRepository state/Commited state.
4)Modified:
------------
-Any file which is already trackedby git , but it is modified in working directory is said to be Modified state.

